Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Figure. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Fourteen words, two centuries (cover; animated version in ",
 StyleBox["docs/images/hero.gif",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "). Each panel projects one word's per-decade ",
 "vector \[Dash] blue in the 1800s, red in the 1990s \[Dash] into a 2-D map \
of its ",
 "own changing neighbourhood. \[Section]5 lets you explore any of the words \
interactively."
}], "Caption",
 CellMargins->{{55, 55}, {2, 
  16}},ExpressionUUID->"c40bd938-1e35-4e70-834a-32de66ecce6a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Word meanings move. ",
 StyleBox["Gay",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " once meant carefree; ",
 StyleBox["broadcast",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " meant to scatter seed by hand; a ",
 StyleBox["computer",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " was a person who did ",
 "arithmetic. This notebook makes that motion visible and measurable. Using \
the ",
 StyleBox["HistWords",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " embeddings (word2vec / SGNS trained on the Google N-grams ",
 "English corpus, one model per decade from the 1800s to the 1990s), we bring \
two ",
 "centuries of independently-trained vector spaces into a single comparable \
frame ",
 "with ",
 StyleBox["orthogonal Procrustes alignment",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ", then trace individual words ",
 "as ",
 StyleBox["trajectories",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " through a 2-D projection of that shared space."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {8, 10}},
 FontSize->14,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.96, 0.97, 1.],ExpressionUUID->"5dc3e60c-c288-47c3-9c68-efa3e7cbfcae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The drifting paths are the heart of the post (and \[Section]5 turns ",
 "them into an interactive explorer). We then recover, from the same aligned ",
 "embeddings, the two ",
 StyleBox["statistical laws of semantic change",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " of Hamilton, Leskovec & Jurafsky (2016): frequent words drift more slowly, \
and ",
 "polysemous words drift faster. Everything is computed in the Wolfram \
Language; the ",
 "code and data products are in the companion repository."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {8, 10}},
 FontSize->14,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.96, 0.97, 1.],ExpressionUUID->"673e90d4-0c88-4d10-8fe2-a88a88a9474a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. The idea: words as moving points", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6b035fd4-94cb-404b-a85b-7a582826cc72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["word embedding",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " places every word at a point in a ",
 "high-dimensional space so that words appearing in similar contexts land \
close ",
 "together. Cosine similarity between two vectors then behaves like a \
similarity of ",
 "meaning: in a modern embedding, ",
 StyleBox["king",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " sits near ",
 StyleBox["queen",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["throne",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", far from ",
 StyleBox["pizza",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"2f7da043-ae7b-455a-9fe3-fc5b51c5ea68"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now train one embedding on text from the 1850s and another on text from ",
 "the 1990s. A word whose meaning has changed will sit in a different \
neighbourhood ",
 "on the two maps. ",
 StyleBox["Gay",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " keeps company with ",
 "cheerful, merry, ",
 "lively",
 " in the 1850s and with ",
 StyleBox["homosexual, lesbian, bisexual",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " in the 1990s. If we can line the two maps up, that change becomes a \
displacement "
}], "we can draw \[Dash] and across twenty decades, a path.", \
"Text",ExpressionUUID->"b0fbd35c-4e2b-4855-aa53-acefebf72f79"],

Cell[BoxData[
 CellMargins -> {{50, 50}, {6, 6}}], "Input",
 CellLabel->" In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b9737e31-ddb0-48c8-a39c-aed09f229c07"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Takeaway.  ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Meaning change shows up as a word ",
 StyleBox["moving",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " relative to the rest of the vocabulary. The whole project is about \
measuring and ",
 "drawing that motion honestly."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {8, 12}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.35, 0.6, 0.4],
 FontSize->12,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.93, 0.97, 0.93],ExpressionUUID->"c9ab1fea-6e59-4df5-82e3-2c7d76112fcd"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. The data: HistWords decade embeddings", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5cc01602-9ef1-4655-a760-6764b83578ce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We use the ",
 StyleBox["HistWords",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " embeddings of Hamilton et al.: ",
 "300-dimensional skip-gram-with-negative-sampling (SGNS) vectors, trained ",
 "separately for each decade on the Google N-grams ",
 StyleBox["eng-all",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " corpus, ",
 "from the 1800s through the 1990s \[Dash] twenty decade-models, each with a ",
 "100,000-word vocabulary. The vectors are L2-normalized; a word absent from \
a ",
 "decade is stored as a zero vector and skipped. The raw download is ~1.6 GB \
and is ",
 "not committed; a thin Python shim converts the NumPy/pickle files to plain \
float32 ",
 "binaries, and everything downstream is Wolfram Language."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"ae1e8bfa-5cf2-4d64-af6b-7d19bb64752b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Coverage varies by word. Of the fourteen we track, ",
 StyleBox["gay",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["awful",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["literally",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["nice",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["mouse",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["web",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " appear in all twenty decades; ",
 StyleBox["queer",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " from the 1830s, ",
 StyleBox["broadcast",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " from the 1850s, and ",
 StyleBox["computer",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " at 1900 (the human-\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]computer\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
sense) ",
 "then continuously from the 1940s (the machine). Gaps are drawn as dashed \
segments."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"914d6f35-c5d3-4203-b227-19c9322684e1"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Why the decades must be aligned", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c21756bb-474b-4eaa-93e3-1157430564a5"],

Cell["\<\
Each decade's embedding is trained independently, so its coordinate axes are \
arbitrary: two decade-maps can be rotated and reflected relative to one \
another even when they agree perfectly about which words are near which. (A \
skip-gram objective is invariant under any orthogonal transformation of the \
space, so nothing pins down a shared orientation.) Before a word can be \
tracked through time, the decades must be rotated into a common frame.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"b7b46359-b4c1-4b64-a0af-63455060a7d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We use ",
 StyleBox["orthogonal Procrustes alignment",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ". Let ",
 StyleBox["A",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " hold the vectors of the 5,000 highest-frequency words present in every \
decade, for ",
 "one decade, and ",
 StyleBox["B",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " the same words in the 1990s reference. We seek the ",
 "orthogonal ",
 StyleBox["R",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " minimising"
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"4877172c-b51d-4caf-9fdf-e7e9608f4bc4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["argmin", 
    StyleBox["R",
     FontSlant->Italic]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
    "\[LeftDoubleBracketingBar]", "A", " ", "R", " ", "-", " ", "B", 
     "\[RightDoubleBracketingBar]"}], "2"], " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"subject", "\[ThinSpace]", "to"}], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["R", "T"], "R", "=", "I"}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellMargins->{{80, 50}, {8, 
  8}},ExpressionUUID->"533c5f59-d4eb-47b4-83fa-0633c90e6659"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This has a closed form from a singular value decomposition: if ",
 StyleBox["U S V",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "\[Transpose] = ",
 StyleBox["A",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "\[Transpose]",
 StyleBox["B",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", then ",
 StyleBox["R",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " = ",
 StyleBox["U V",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "\[Transpose]",
 ". Because ",
 StyleBox["R",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " is orthogonal it preserves every length and angle ",
 StyleBox["within",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " a decade \[Dash] it only reorients the space \[Dash] so each decade's \
nearest ",
 "neighbours are exactly as trained, while becoming comparable ",
 StyleBox["across",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " decades. (Nearest-neighbour queries in \[Section]6 are therefore run in \
each ",
 "decade's own native space; alignment is needed only to compare frames.)"
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"d19a9a46-473f-40b9-9dd1-0cb4527fcef9"],

