Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Takeaway.  ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Trajectories can be cross-checked against plain word lists. When the ",
 "neighbours of ",
 StyleBox["broadcast",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " go from ",
 StyleBox["sow, scatter",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["radio, television",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", the drawn path is just reporting that shift."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {8, 12}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.35, 0.6, 0.4],
 FontSize->12,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.93, 0.97, 0.93],ExpressionUUID->"50c80831-7bf3-4314-9d20-8d9bf63c734f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["7. Two statistical laws of semantic change", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"23993ddd-7907-48cb-abb8-b1ed71556f54"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Hamilton, Leskovec & Jurafsky (2016) report two regularities that hold ",
 "across languages and corpora. Both fall out of the same aligned embeddings, \
measured ",
 "over the ",
 StyleBox["8,806",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " dictionary content words present in every decade ",
 "(function words and archaic/foreign tokens removed via a stoplist and \
WordNet ",
 "membership). A word's ",
 StyleBox["rate of change",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " is the mean cosine distance ",
 "between its aligned vectors in consecutive decades."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"f0c6efdf-77eb-4183-95af-8768fb646ec3"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The law of conformity", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"adc649b6-c190-48c6-92ce-bcd6975ab0e4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["More frequent words change more slowly.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Plotting log change-rate ",
 "against a frequency proxy gives a clear negative trend (slope \[TildeTilde] \
",
 "\[Minus]0.045, Pearson r \[TildeTilde] \[Minus]0.21). ",
 StyleBox["Why:",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " a high-frequency word appears in a huge range of contexts, so its vector \
is an ",
 "average over many uses and is statistically well-anchored; rare words are \
estimated ",
 "from little data and are free to wander."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"94498e6e-b715-466f-b234-cabd512532d7"],

