Cell["\<\
The effect sizes are modest \[Dash] one corpus, English only, and a \
rank-based frequency proxy \[Dash] but both signs reproduce the published \
laws, from an independent re-implementation.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"5b6cabed-e6a0-48fb-a3f5-66a20930ff93"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["8. The most-drifted words \[Dash] and a caveat", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"67499c04-b88c-4a79-b469-7d6b5b54068e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Ranking every stable content word by how far it moved between its 1800s and \
",
 "1990s aligned vectors surfaces two phenomena at once. Some entries are \
genuine ",
 "meaning change (",
 StyleBox["advert",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " verb \[Rule] noun, ",
 StyleBox["peer",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " noble \[Rule] equal, ",
 StyleBox["media",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["broadcast",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "); others are lexical obsolescence or register shift, where an archaic word \
(",
 StyleBox["twelvemonth, fourthly, civilities",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ") simply stopped occurring in the same ",
 "kinds of text. A large embedding displacement means ",
 "\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]the contexts changed\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \[Dash] \
which is ",
 "necessary, but not sufficient, for \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]the meaning ",
 "changed\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. Distinguishing the two is where embeddings \
end and ",
 "lexicography begins."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"7aa683c0-1054-4a9f-b2be-a9c2dde89541"],

